      "claim": "Water has a much higher specific heat capacity than land, so the temperature of the ocean changes only slowly over daily and seasonal cycles.",
      "evidence": "Specific heat of liquid water ≈ 4.18 J·g⁻¹·°C⁻¹; dry soil/rock ≈ 0.8–1.0 J·g⁻¹·°C⁻¹. For the same energy input, ΔT = Q/(m c) is far smaller for water.",
