      "id": 2,
      "claim": "The air directly above the ocean equilibrates with the ocean’s relatively constant temperature, creating maritime air masses that are thermally stable.",
      "evidence": "Heat exchange between water surface and the overlying air (conduction, convection, latent heat) quickly brings the lowest few meters of air to near‑water temperature; this is observed in sea‑breeze formation.",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
