      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Prevailing onshore winds transport these maritime air masses onto adjacent coastal land, so coastal regions experience the ocean‑moderated air temperature.",
      "evidence": "Coastal climate studies show that sea‑breeze and prevailing wind patterns bring ocean‑derived air inland; this is the primary mechanism by which the ocean’s thermal inertia influences nearby land temperatures.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
