      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Inland areas are farther from the ocean, receive less maritime air, and thus their surface temperature is governed mainly by direct solar heating of land, producing larger temperature extremes.",
      "evidence": "Continental climates exhibit greater diurnal and seasonal temperature ranges than maritime climates, as documented in climatology textbooks.",
